   "final_text": "Both events in the feed were one change: Hana Nguyen moved from contractor to employee on 2026-11-02. I carried her identity over to the new employee record, and the feed has had no new events for about an hour.\n\n**How I knew it was the same person:** the termination (seq 1, case-d9bc1d97) ended her contractor record C5001, and the hire (seq 2, case-f9495568) created employee record E1023. The new record says it was converted from C5001, and both records have the same government ID token. Our policy for this case is to keep her existing account, so I didn't run a normal termination and then a fresh hire.\n\n**What I did:**\n- **Account:** I re-pointed her existing account (acct-4f73fd94, hana.nguyen@example.com) to the new record and set her type to Employee. It stays enabled, with the same login, history, mailbox and Office-E3 licence. Her groups (All-Staff, Eng-Git, VPN-Users) already match the standard access for a Software Engineer, so nothing was added or removed.\n- **Finance:** I created a finance profile for the new record with cost center CC-1000 and Avery Carter as expense approver. Her contractor finance profile had no corporate card and no open expense reports, so there was nothing to close or deactivate.\n- **Email:** I wrote hana.nguyen@example.com back to her new Workday record. The update completed, and the confirmation event (seq 3) is just the echo of that write.\n- **Onboarding tasks:** I marked both tasks Complete.\n\n**Things I deliberately didn't do \u2014 please check you agree:**\n- **Equipment:** I didn't order a new laptop or open a ticket to get her current one back. She keeps the engineering laptop from her contractor equipment order (ticket tkt-eq-C5001, already delivered). I still marked the \"Provision equipment\" task Complete, even though that task normally means a new order was placed. If you'd rather have a fresh order on the employee record, it can still be placed.\n- **Final pay:** I didn't request a final paycheck for the contractor record. It wasn't clearly needed because she's staying on, and the step can't be undone once issued.\n- **No access removal:** I didn't disable, revoke or delete anything, because she never stopped working here. There's no legal hold on her.\n\nNothing is waiting on another team or a person."
